  "notes": [
    "অ is the first independent vowel in the Bengali alphabet. Its sound is commonly written ô in learner transliteration and is similar to the first vowel sound in the British pronunciation of “often.”",
    "Unlike most other Bengali vowels, অ has no separate vowel mark (কার). After a consonant with no visible vowel sign, an inherent অ-like sound is often understood: ক is read kô.",
    "In natural speech, the exact sound of অ can vary slightly by word and dialect. Use the audio controls to imitate a Bengali voice."
